  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Set an annual overall migration limit with quotas for refugees, process asylum claims outside the UK, and seek national control over asylum rules including changes to international/EU frameworks; 24/7 port surveillance, restore embarkation controls, and create a Border Control Police; end early release, add 20,000 prison places, recruit more police, and introduce elected police commissioners; EU referendum on the Constitutional Treaty, keep the pound, and repatriate fisheries control; restore school discipline with stronger powers for heads; appoint a Homeland Security Minister and strengthen counter‑terror capabilities. TEXT_D: Allow asylum seekers to work and pursue EU common standards; Single Equality Act and hate‑crime units in every force; repeal flawed terror provisions, protect jury trial, and tighten judicial control of control orders; support EU reform and prepare for euro entry; strong environmental agenda including a Carbon Tax, a 20% renewables target, zero‑waste goals, and opposition to new nuclear plants.",
